Rāma blessed by his mother proceeds to Sītā awaiting consecration --- Rāma lights the crowded royal road delighting hearts by virtues --- Sītā rises trembling seeing gloomy sweating distracted Rāma --- Sītā asks why Puṣya passes without umbrella chowries bards and crowning rites --- Sītā asks why no gold chariot elephant throne or cheering people --- Rāma reveals Daśaratha must honor two boons granted to Kaikēyī --- Rāma announces fourteen Daṇḍaka years and Bharata appointed prince --- Rāma bids Sītā never praise him before prosperous Bharata --- Rāma bids observe vows fasts and honor aged parents and mothers --- Rāma bids honor Lakṣmaṇa Śatrughna and never offend King Bharata
